# headless-erp — Cursor rules (always on)

You are building a multi-tenant SaaS re-implementation of ERPNext's default behaviour. The plan is law:
read `docs/PLAN.md` first, then the relevant `docs/architecture/*.md`, then `docs/modules/NN-<module>.md` for the
module you touch. If the task conflicts with the plan, stop and say so before coding. Update the docs when behaviour changes.

## Source of truth
- ERPNext clone: `C:\Users\John\Desktop\erpnext` (branch develop). Port *default* behaviour only. Cite the ERPNext
  file(s) you read in the PR/commit body. Use `scripts/erpnext-doctype.ps1 -Names "<DocType>"` to read schemas.
- Keep ERPNext field names, status labels, naming-series prefixes and default values unless the plan says otherwise.
- Out of scope (do not build): CRM, Support, Quality, POS, Loyalty, Subscriptions, Website, Regional/e-invoicing,
  HR/Payroll, Pricing Rules, Item Variants, Accounting Dimensions, Deferred accounting, Period Closing, Repost tools.

## Stack (fixed)
Next.js 16.4+ App Router (React 19, TS strict, Turbopack, `cacheComponents` on, `proxy.ts`), Supabase (Postgres, Auth via
`@supabase/ssr`, Storage, pg_cron), Zustand (UI/session state only), Untitled UI React (Tailwind v4 + React Aria,
components copied into `src/components/base|application`), Recharts 3, Zod, React Hook Form, TanStack Table, nuqs,
Biome, Vitest, pgTAP, Playwright, GitHub Actions → Netlify.

## Non-negotiables
1. Every tenant table has `org_id` and RLS enabled + policies (see `docs/architecture/01-tenancy-auth-rls.md`). No
   migration without RLS. Ledger tables are append-only; cancel = reversal rows + the
   `is_cancelled`/`delinked` flag on the cancelled voucher's rows (the only allowed update).
2. All ledger/status/numbering mutations happen in `app.*` Postgres functions called from Server Actions
   (`app.submit_doc`, `app.cancel_doc`, `app.amend_doc`, `app.save_doc`). Never write `gl_entry`,
   `stock_ledger_entry`, `payment_ledger_entry`, `bin` from TypeScript.
3. Server authorization uses `supabase.auth.getClaims()`; never `getSession()` on the server; never import the
   service-role client outside `server-only` modules (provisioning, cron, tests).
4. Money/qty are `numeric` in SQL; rounding via `app.round()` / `src/lib/calc/number.ts`. Client totals are previews;
   the server recomputes before posting.
5. One doctype = one migration (+RLS +doctype_meta +role_permissions) + `src/doctypes/<module>/<slug>.ts` descriptor +
   Zod schema + Server Actions + list/form UI + tests. Regenerate `src/types/database.ts` after schema changes.
6. `params`, `searchParams`, `cookies()`, `headers()` are async — always `await`. Default to Server Components;
   `'use client'` only for interactive leaves (forms, tables, charts, stores).
7. UI: Untitled UI tokens only (no raw hex), compact density, keyboard-first, tabular numerals, empty/loading/error
   states for every list/form. No new dependency without a note in `docs/PLAN.md §2`.
8. Small commits (one doctype or one engine function). Conventional commits. Never commit secrets or tenant data.

## Working style
- Before coding a doctype: read its ERPNext `.json` + `.py` (+ `test_*.py` for expected ledger output), summarise the
  ported fields/behaviour and deviations in the module doc, then implement.
- Prefer editing existing generic components (`DocList`, `DocForm`, `ChildTable`, `ReportView`, `DashboardView`)
  over one-off pages. Add a descriptor, not a bespoke screen.
- Use the Supabase MCP for `apply_migration` (local/dev only), `execute_sql` (reads), `get_advisors`
  (must be clean), `generate_typescript_types`. Production changes go through CI only.
- Hosted Supabase is the dev project only. Load `.env.local` without echoing it and clear the variables afterwards.
  `db reset --linked` only when the project should be wiped; the local `supabase db reset` job runs in GitHub Actions.

## Workflow (every PR)
Never commit to `main`. One doctype or one engine function per PR, in this order:
1. Branch from `origin/main`.
2. Read the ERPNext `.json`/`.py`/`test_*.py`; note ported fields and deviations in the module doc.
3. Migration (RLS + `doctype_meta` + `role_permissions`), then `npx supabase db push --linked --include-all --yes`.
4. pgTAP file for the change, then `npm run db:test:linked` for the whole `supabase/tests` suite.
5. `npm run db:types:linked`, then `node scripts/check-types.mjs --linked`.
6. Descriptor, registry, queries/mutations, UI.
7. `npx biome check --write .`, then `npx biome ci .`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run test:db`, `npm run build`.
8. The PR's own Playwright spec plus related specs via `npm run e2e`.
9. `get_advisors` clean (accepted: `rls_auto_enable`, `auth_leaked_password_protection`).
10. Docs in the same PR: module doc Built note and deviations, §10 checklist tick, `docs/PLAN.md` if scope moved.
11. Commit with a message file (cite ERPNext files), `gh pr create --body-file`, `gh pr checks <n> --watch`,
    `gh pr merge <n> --squash`, delete the branch, `git branch -f main origin/main`.

## Phase gate
A phase is finished only when: every item in the module doc §10 checklist is ticked or re-homed to a named phase;
its critical flows have Playwright specs; the full `npm run e2e` and `npm run db:test:linked` pass; and its
`docs/PLAN.md` §7 row is marked Complete with the date.
